 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20speak=20CLI,=20return=20data,=20and=20find=20things?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A hands-on review against the live 199-entity Sanity UI document, worked
through in severity order. Two of the findings were data bugs that had
been quietly degrading both surfaces.

The CLI still spoke MCP. Handler prose names tools canonically, so
`dsds brief build` — the first command the generated AGENTS.md tells an
agent to run — carried 16 `dsds_*` names and "Each step uses a tool from
this MCP server", and the unconfigured-setup copy explained how to edit
an MCP client's env block while wrongly telling CLI users that relative
paths are unsupported. src/vocabulary.js renders the core's canonical
text per transport: MCP is unchanged, the CLI reads as a CLI, and a new
porcelain command costs one line in CLI_EQUIVALENTS.

--json returned prose. Every read command put a markdown document in
`data`, so the advertised `| jq -r .data` handed back markdown and
`.data.entities[].identifier` was impossible. list and search now emit
structuredContent; `data` carries it and the rendering moves to `text`.
BREAKING: lint's findings move from `structured` to `data`.

Two symptoms, one root cause: summarizeEntities read metadata.summary
only, but real 0.20.0 keeps the one-liner in `description`. All 199
summary cells rendered blank, and search — which indexes that field —
could only ever match identifiers and names. The fallback fixes both.

Search was one substring match over the whole query, so "primary button"
always returned nothing. Terms are tokenized and ANDed across
identifier, name, summary, tags and kind, results are ranked, and a dead
end names the word that found nothing.

Also: Damerau-Levenshtein "did you mean" wherever a name can be
mistyped (a typo'd identifier used to print all 199 on one unwrapped
line), suggestions for flags, commands, kinds, statuses, block names and
tool names, -h/-v, --limit on list and search, dsds completion for
bash/zsh/fish, manifest --compact (38KB to 13KB), lint --apply
--dry-run, "Uncategorized" in place of the heading "Undefineds", block
lists deduped and including `api`, cwd-relative paths in output, and one
fewer redundant stderr warning.

398 dsds-mcp + 144 dsds-cli tests green. Verified over the real MCP
protocol: instructions stay MCP-flavored, the data fixes reach both.

